.Dd July 7, 2026
.Dt DIFFWISE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm diffwise
.Nd export jj commits as patch files for code review
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r Ar revset
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
exports a series of
.Xr jj 1
commits as patch files, one file per commit, for mailing-list style
code review: the reviewer opens a patch file and replies inline.
.Pp
By default
.Nm
exports the commits selected by the revset
.Ql ::@ & mutable() ,
the working copy and its mutable ancestors.
A different revset can be given with
.Fl r .
.Pp
Commits are written oldest first into the current directory.
Each patch file contains an mbox-style
.Ql From
line carrying the commit id, followed by
.Ql From ,
.Ql Date ,
and
.Ql Subject
headers taken from the commit author and description, the remainder
of the commit description if any, and a
.Ql ---
separator line followed by the commit's changes in git diff format.
When more than one commit is selected, subjects are numbered
.Ql [PATCH n/m] .
.Pp
Files are named
.Pa NNNN-subject.patch ,
where
.Pa NNNN
is the position of the commit in the series counting from 0001 and
.Pa subject
is the first line of the commit description with runs of characters
other than letters and digits replaced by a single hyphen.
A commit with no description produces a patch with an empty subject
and a file named
.Pa NNNN-patch.patch .
A revset that selects no commits produces no files.
The path of each file is printed to standard output as it is
written.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width "-r revset"
.It Fl r Ar revset
Export the commits selected by
.Ar revset
instead of the default
.Ql ::@ & mutable() .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Export the working copy and its mutable ancestors, one patch file
per commit, into the current directory:
.Dl % diffwise
.Pp
Export two specific commits:
.Dl % diffwise -r 'wqnwkozp | tmzuqxpv'
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jj 1
